        "raw_output": "{\n  \"slots\": [\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"music_history\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_419ccfcd7f3577a641bd2d8d\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user has a deep emotional connection to music but has struggled with technical and analytical approaches. They explored various genres and attended festivals (including an electronic music festival in 2017), but found music theory and historical research tedious and overwhelming (2018, 2020). They enjoy attending live performances, discovering album artwork and lyrics, creating mood-based playlists, and blending natural sounds with melody in their own compositions. They have created music incorporating field recordings from nature, which rejuvenated their passion. They have considered composing original music and collaborating with other musicians. They value personal, emotional engagement over passive consumption or technical dissection.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s34\",\"s35\",\"s11\",\"s12\",\"s43\",\"s22\",\"s13\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s24\",\"s45\",\"s23\",\"s14\",\"s44\",\"s10\",\"s26\",\"s25\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"past\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user's statements across multiple conversations consistently describe a preference for emotional and experiential engagement with music over technical analysis. They report attending an electronic music festival in 2017 (s22-s23), finding music theory unappealing in 2018 (s24-s25), trying historical music research in 2020 but finding it tedious (s10-s11), enjoying live performances and album artwork/lyrics (s13-s14), creating music with nature field recordings (s43-s45), and feeling that passive consumption is less fulfilling than personal creation (s34-s35). They also expressed that diving too deep into technical aspects became a chore (s3) and that the essence of their love for music is emotional connection (s4).\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"current_constraints\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_c705502daeea10cabc099a4c\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user has moved away from technical, analytical approaches to music (music theory, audio production, historical research) because they felt like chores and diminished joy. They now prefer emotionally connected, personal, and creative engagement: composing original tracks, exploring genres and cultural significance, attending live performances, discovering album artwork/lyrics/stories, and making mood-based playlists. They have also found fulfillment in creating music that connects with their heritage and personal identity.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s11\",\"s12\",\"s76\",\"s13\",\"s4\",\"s3\",\"s53\",\"s77\",\"s14\",\"s10\",\"s73\",\"s54\",\"s75\",\"s74\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"current\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"Multiple user statements across conversations consistently describe abandoning technical/analytical music activities (theory, production, historical research) due to loss of joy, and instead adopting emotionally resonant, creative, and culturally connected forms of engagement such as composing, attending live shows, exploring genres and stories, and creating heritage-inspired music.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"goals_values\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_9de115f693135beabba365d0\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user values personal fulfillment and creative expression through music that is emotionally connected, personally meaningful, and rooted in heritage, while avoiding overly technical or structured approaches that feel like a chore. They seek deeper engagement through exploring genres, cultural significance, live performances, album artwork and lyrics, making playlists, blending traditional roots with modern sounds, and developing an app to help others do the same. They prioritize joy, emotional connection, and self-discovery over analytical or passive consumption.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s34\",\"s35\",\"s11\",\"s62\",\"s12\",\"s61\",\"s13\",\"s4\",\"s63\",\"s3\",\"s53\",\"s14\",\"s10\",\"s54\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"current\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user explicitly states that diving too deep into technical aspects became a chore and that the essence of their love for music lies in emotional connection rather than analytical components (s3, s4). They found researching historical music trends tedious and overwhelming, preferring a less structured approach (s10, s11, s12). They describe engaging with music through genres, cultural significance, live performances, album artwork, lyrics, and playlists as more fulfilling (s13, s14). They express disappointment with a documentary that skimmed over the artistic process, and reflect that true connection comes from deeper engagement and personal creation (s34, s35). They later describe connecting with their roots through music, expressing identity and family history (s53, s54). Finally, they are blending traditional musical roots with modern sounds and developing an app to empower others to do the same (s61, s62, s63). These statements collectively support the user's current goals and values regarding personal fulfillment and creative expression.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"response\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"obs_response_1\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"Collaborating with others who share your musical interests can also be a rewarding path. A user found fulfillment through working with musicians from diverse backgrounds, mixing traditional and electronic elements to expand their creative horizons. Such group efforts can enhance not only your musical explorations but also build lasting relationships, as you contribute unique perspectives to a collective musical vision.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s61\",\"s62\",\"s63\",\"s53\",\"s54\",\"s43\",\"s44\",\"s45\",\"s13\",\"s14\",\"s34\",\"s35\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"current\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {\n            \"music_history\": 1,\n            \"current_constraints\": 1,\n            \"goals_values\": 1\n          },\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user's history shows they value emotional, creative, and heritage-connected music expression, and have already begun blending traditional roots with modern sounds (s61-s63) and creating music with nature field recordings (s43-s45). They enjoy live performances and exploring cultural significance (s13-s14), and find fulfillment in personal creation over passive consumption (s34-s35). Option (c) directly aligns with these values by suggesting collaboration to mix traditional and electronic elements, which matches the user's current project of blending roots with modern sounds and developing an app to help others do the same. The other options are less aligned: (a) is too generic and does not match the user's active creative direction; (b) focuses on sound engineering and technical remixing, which the user has explicitly moved away from; (d) involves music criticism and writing reviews, which is analytical and passive, contrary to the user's preference for active creation and emotional connection.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}",
